Abhirup, thanks for your use of NIMBLE and sending your question to the list.  Right off hand I don't know why the block sampler isn't updating, but replacing the block sampler with 100 univariate RW samplers on the w[i] terms shows good mixing.  You can do that via:

gpconf <- configureMCMC(CgpModel, print=TRUE)

##### changes begin here
gpconf$removeSamplers('w')
for(node in gpModel$expandNodeNames('w', returnScalarComponents=TRUE)) {
    gpconf$addSampler(node, 'RW')
}
gpconf$printSamplers()
##### changes end here

gpconf$addMonitors(c('w'))
gpMCMC <- buildMCMC(gpconf)
CgpMCMC <- compileNimble(gpMCMC, project = CgpModel)

Then the sampling looks good for the w[i] terms.

Let us know how that works for you.

Daniel

