Subject: How to save posterior iterations portion by portion?
Message-ID: <rPRMQYCSqhg.TkX9YQDmCQAJ@nimble-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/nimble-users/c/rPRMQYCSqhg/m/TkX9YQDmCQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi all,
May I know if there's an equivalent function in nimble to save the chain of iteration portion and keep on producing more iterations? Like the jags function "update()"? In jags, I have something like below:
## the jags model first
mod <- jags(data, parameters.to.save, model.file, n.chains, n.iter)
model.update <- mod
save(model.update)

  #--- update MCMC ----------
    for (i in 2:N.STEPS) {

      model.update <- update(model.update,
                             parameters.to.save, n.iter)
      save(model.update)
    }#end of i loop (steps)

The code above updates MCMC and save some iterations at multiple times.

Thanks.
Fengqing

From uc9e9cbbfb3b043f0 at groups.google.com  Tue Nov 22 15:44:48 2016
From: uc9e9cbbfb3b043f0 at groups.google.com (Daniel Turek)
